00:00:02.935 --> 00:00:05.171 align:start size:59% position:41%
I didn't even know
this place existed.

00:00:05.204 --> 00:00:08.374 align:start size:91% position:9%
- I'm gonna have
  my birthday party here.
- Yeah.

00:00:08.407 --> 00:00:10.443
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:00:10.476 --> 00:00:13.446 line:0%
Marques invited me to this
incredible vintage warehouse

00:00:13.479 --> 00:00:17.384 line:0%
that has all kinds
of old Mac computers.

00:00:19.151 --> 00:00:22.121
<i> Specifically, the 1984 Mac,
 which is something</i>

00:00:22.154 --> 00:00:23.389
that has a very special place
in my heart.

00:00:23.422 --> 00:00:25.725
- Yeah, it's good.
- It's so great.

00:00:25.758 --> 00:00:27.293 align:start position:0%
They don't make 'em
like they used to.

00:00:27.326 --> 00:00:28.795 align:start size:75% position:25%
Do you wanna open it up?

00:00:32.331 --> 00:00:34.400
So there are a few screws here.

00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:38.137 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Should we go for it?
- I think we should
  take it apart.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:39.539 align:start size:41% position:59%
( muttering )

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:43.376 align:start position:0%
All right, final screw.

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:45.411 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Okay.
- Let's lift this off.

00:00:45.444 --> 00:00:49.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do not touch the CRT coil
because you might get shocked.

00:00:49.348 --> 00:00:51.517 align:start position:0%
Okay,
inside is the CRT monitor.

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.854 align:start size:84% position:16%
- It goes kinda far
  into the body of it.
- Don't touch.

00:00:54.887 --> 00:00:57.090 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Okay, I'm not gonna
  touch the CRT coil.
- Don't. Mm-mm.

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:58.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
- I'll hold the bottom down.
- Okay.

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:01.428 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Ready?
- Yeah, yeah. Moment of truth.

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:05.431 align:start size:69% position:31%
Oh, man, look at this.

00:01:05.464 --> 00:01:10.269 align:start position:0%
That is the inside
of a 1984 Mac.

00:01:10.302 --> 00:01:12.505 align:start position:0%
That's the coil.
Don't touch the CRT.

00:01:12.538 --> 00:01:14.407 align:start position:0%
There are two
different boards.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:17.276 align:start position:0%
There's, to me unrecognizable,
mostly power components.

00:01:17.309 --> 00:01:20.113 align:start position:0%
And then there's also a board
back here at the bottom,

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:22.548 align:start position:0%
which has
a lot more soldering.

00:01:22.581 --> 00:01:25.351 align:start size:91% position:9%
- That's the floppy drive.
- The system disk
  is the floppy disk,

00:01:25.384 --> 00:01:26.853 align:start size:69% position:31%
so that basically
loads it into the RAM.

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:28.721 size:78% position:61%
And as soon as you take
that disk out, it's gone.

00:01:28.754 --> 00:01:30.890 align:start size:81% position:19%
You're basically
loading things as it goes.

00:01:30.923 --> 00:01:33.726
And it would be
a combination of reading

00:01:33.759 --> 00:01:36.429 align:start position:0%
from the memory that it
has preloaded things into

00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:38.264 align:start position:0%
and that floppy disk.

00:01:38.297 --> 00:01:41.734 align:start size:81% position:19%
This only had 128K of RAM.

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:43.636 align:start position:0%
What, now it's
a thousand times smaller?

00:01:43.669 --> 00:01:45.638 align:start size:72% position:28%
One front facing selfie
on the iPhone,

00:01:45.671 --> 00:01:47.240 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Yeah?
- you couldn't even
  fit it on here.

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:49.609 align:start size:63% position:38%
Like, that's insane.

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:52.678
<i> Steve Jobs had created this
 as a work of art.</i>

00:01:52.711 --> 00:01:55.648
So, in most art,
people sign them.

00:01:55.681 --> 00:01:58.518 align:start size:81% position:19%
- True.
- So, inside of here
  are autographs

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:01.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
- of all the people
  that worked on this team.
- Oh, that's cool.

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:03.289 align:start size:84% position:16%
- So you can see them
  right there.
- And they're subtle.

00:02:03.322 --> 00:02:04.790 align:start position:0%
All these little
inscriptions.

00:02:04.823 --> 00:02:07.160 align:start position:0%
That's actually
a nice little touch,
signing your work.

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:08.694 align:start position:0%
I'm glad we learned
all this today.

00:02:08.727 --> 00:02:10.696 align:start position:0%
Thank you so much
for helping me
take apart this Mac

00:02:10.729 --> 00:02:12.765 align:start position:0%
and for giving me
the breakdown.

00:02:12.798 --> 00:02:13.833 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Appreciate it.
- Thank you so much.

00:02:13.866 --> 00:02:15.335 align:start size:63% position:38%
This was seriously
amazing. Wow.

